\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The distance $r_{\mathrm  {same}}$ at which half of document pairs are judged the same specific content, interpolated between bins of about 40 pairs, under Qwen3.8-27B (Q) and Gemma-4-31B-it (G), and the sample size the collapse law prescribes for an isolation rate of 0.5 at that distance, rounded. In parentheses, the empirical sample size where the grid of 100 to 7{,}000 reaches the target. On Bluesky fewer than half of the pairs closer than 0.1 are judged the same content under either judge, so no distance qualifies.}}{8}{table.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rcal}{{4}{8}{The distance $r_{\mathrm {same}}$ at which half of document pairs are judged the same specific content, interpolated between bins of about 40 pairs, under Qwen3.8-27B (Q) and Gemma-4-31B-it (G), and the sample size the collapse law prescribes for an isolation rate of 0.5 at that distance, rounded. In parentheses, the empirical sample size where the grid of 100 to 7{,}000 reaches the target. On Bluesky fewer than half of the pairs closer than 0.1 are judged the same content under either judge, so no distance qualifies}{table.caption.5}{}}
